course: dictionary
lesson: 12509
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Depress» can mean to make someone feel very sad, or to press something down. Look at the words near it to decide.
explain: «The rainy weather depresses me» is about feelings: the rain makes me feel low. «Depress the brake pedal» is about pushing with your foot. Ask yourself: is this about a feeling, or about pushing?
explain: The word can also be about money. «A bad year depresses sales» means the year makes sales go lower. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Depress means to make someone feel very sad and without hope.
fact: To depress a button, key or pedal means to press it down, as in «Depress the brake pedal to stop.»
fact: To depress prices, trade or wages means to make them lower or less active.
fact: Depressed means feeling very low; it is also the name of an illness called depression that needs care from a grown-up or a doctor.
fact: Depressing is an adjective that means making you feel sad, as in «The grey, rainy day was depressing.»
exercise: «The news about the storm depressed everyone in the village.» What does depressed mean here? | *Made everyone feel very sad | Made everyone very hungry | Made everyone very tall | Pressed everyone down onto the ground
exercise: «Please depress the red button to start the machine.» What does depress mean here? | *Press down | Hide from view | Make prices lower | Feel very sad
exercise: «A bad winter depressed sales for the little shop.» What does depressed mean here? | Pressed down with a hand | Made very happy | Made very loud | *Made lower or less active
test: «The gloomy film was so depressing that Sam switched it off.» What does depressing mean? | Very loud and noisy | Making you laugh out loud | *Making you feel sad | Very cheap to buy
test: Mum says, «Depress the pedal gently, love.» What should you do to the pedal? | *Press it down | Count how many times it moves | Paint it a new colour | Lift it up and away
exam: Which sentence uses depress to mean press down? | «The bad year depressed wages.» | «The rain depresses me.» | *«Depress the green key to save your work.» | «The sad song depressed the whole class.»
